3D models (models/)
  - Mars globe, 2001 Mars Odyssey, Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter,
    Apollo Lunar Module, Viking Lander, Mars Exploration Rover, Curiosity:
    NASA 3D Resources (https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/; mirror: https://github.com/nasa/NASA-3D-Resources).
  - InSight lander (deployed): NASA/JPL-Caltech.
    NASA material is generally not subject to copyright in the United States.
    Credit NASA and do not imply NASA endorsement (NASA Images and Media
    Usage Guidelines: https://www.nasa.gov/nasa-brand-center/images-and-media/).
  - Moon globe (models/planets/moon_small.glb): NASA Scientific Visualization Studio,
    "Moon 3D Models for Web, AR, and Animation" (2026), https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/14959/
  - Mars globe source page: NASA/JPL-Caltech, "Planet Mars, 3D Model" (2019),
    https://science.nasa.gov/resource/planet-mars-3d-model/
  - Archive photographs (img/archive/, 513 pictures for 115 missions): from the team's
    photo archive; only images credited to NASA or other US government bodies, to ESA,
    or released under an open licence (CC BY, CC BY-SA, CC0, public domain) are
    included. Pictures credited to other agencies or companies, reprocessings by
    private persons and NC/ND-licensed pictures were left out. Each picture keeps its
    credit and a link to the original. The short English captions come from the
    team's archive, which compiled them from the mission pages of azmth.space.
  - The files in models/optimized/ are compressed copies of the originals
    (gltf-transform 4.5.1: meshopt geometry, WebP textures). The originals are unchanged.

Data
  - Moon and Mars mission lists: NASA NSSDCA (lunar timeline, Mars chronology,
    Table of Anthropogenic Impacts and Spacecraft on the Moon), NASA Science,
    NASA/JPL and ESA. Facts are rewritten in our own words with links to sources.
  - Photographs: NASA Image and Video Library (loaded from NASA servers); images
    credited to ESA are (c) ESA and are shown for education with credit.
  - Team photo and the RealPugs pug logo (img/): Team RealPugs.
  - Scientific papers, NASA reports and agency documents are linked, not reproduced.
    Every source is listed on the site's References page with its title, author,
    year, document type and a direct link.
